:47.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577665/uga-defensive-coordinator-schumann-coach-florida-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Aiden Flora, nation's leading rusher, re-signs with Iowa State for next season","description":"Iowa State running back Aiden Flora, who leads the nation in rushing, announced Monday that he has re-signed with the Cyclones for next season.","published":"2026-11-23T23:57:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577520/aiden-flora-nation-leading-rusher-re-signs-iowa-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas A&M names John Thornton interim athletic director effective Dec. 1","description":"John Thornton will take over as interim athletic director at Texas A&M, effective Dec. 1, replacing the departed Trev Alberts.","published":"2026-11-23T22:07:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50576559/texas-names-john-thornton-interim-ad-effective-dec-1","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Giants DC Dennard Wilson interviews for HC job at alma mater Maryland","description":"Giants defensive coordinator Dennard Wilson had a virtual interview recently for the vacant head coaching job at Maryland, sources told NFL Network.","published":"2026-11-23T21:22:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50575838/sources-giants-dennard-wilson-interviews-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LSU's Lane Kiffin apologizes for using profanity during halftime interview","description":"LSU coach Lane Kiffin has apologized for using profanity during a halftime interview with the school's radio network in Saturday's loss to Tennessee.","published":"2026-11-23T20:12:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575735/lsu-kiffin-apologizes-use-profanity-interview","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest leading rusher Ty Clark ruled out for season","description":"Wake Forest running back Ty Clark will miss the rest of the season, coach Jake Dickert announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T20:30:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575731/wake-forest-leading-rusher-ry-clark-ruled-season","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Syracuse rules QB Steve Angeli (shoulder) out vs. Notre Dame","description":"Syracuse has ruled starting quarterback Steve Angeli out for Saturday's game against Notre Dame due to a shoulder injury.","published":"2026-11-23T18:40:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575118/syracuse-rules-qb-steve-angeli-shoulder-vs-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana not yet naming starting QB for game vs. Purdue, Curt Cignetti says","description":"Indiana is not yet naming a starting quarterback for Saturday's rivalry game against Purdue, coach Curt Cignetti said Monday.","published":"2026-11-23T18:51:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575086/indiana-not-yet-naming-starting-qb-game-vs-purdue","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama's Kalen DeBoer expects QB Keelon Russell to be 'full go' vs. Auburn","description":"Alabama coach Kalen DeBoer said Monday that he expects QB Keelon Russell, who is working his way back from an ankle injury, to be \"full go\" for rivalry week against Auburn.","published":"2026-11-23T18:13:53.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50574915/alabama-deboer-expects-qb-russell-full-go-auburn","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5112647/jordan-ross","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan_Ross_(American_football)"},"pick":{"pick":49,"round":2,"team":"LAR","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jordan Ross (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jordan_Ross_(American_football)","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:09Z","intro":"Jordan Destin Ross is an American college football defensive end for the LSU Tigers. He previously played for the Tennessee Volunteers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Ross is from Vestavia Hills, Alabama. He attended Vestavia Hills High School where he played football as a defensive end. As a junior in 2022, he helped Vestavia Hills to the second round of the Class 7A playoffs while posting 49 tackles, 16 tackles-for-loss and 2.5 sacks, as well as scoring two defensive touchdowns. He then totaled 72 tackles, 23 tackles-for-loss and 12.5 sacks as a senior, earning selection to the Under Armour All-America Game. Ross was named the 7A Defensive Player of the Year by Around The State Sports and as the Defensive Player of the Year by the Over the Mountain Journal.\nA five-star recruit, Ross was ranked a top-10 player nationally as well as the best edge rusher in the nation by 247Sports and On3.com. He committed to play college football for the Tennessee Volunteers. He was the highest-ranked member of Tennessee's 2024 recruiting class."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Ross entered his true freshman season in 2024 as a backup defensive end, behind James Pearce Jr., Joshua Josephs and Caleb Herring. He was used mainly on special teams and posted three tackles, 1.5 tackles-for-loss and blocked a punt which he returned for a touchdown, earning selection to the Southeastern Conference (SEC) All-Freshman team. After Pearce graduated, Ross began seeing more significant playing time as a sophomore in the 2025 season."}]}}